From 3f3a845387b8a5f42617f59b35c912e24912dcff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:32:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] misc: sdp-micom: add IR blaster/receiver and IR sender probe
 skeletons (patch 0019)

Add DT nodes for the Samsung SDP Nike-L IR Blaster/Receiver (IRB) and
IR Sender (IRS), and minimal probe-only skeleton drivers.

Hardware values from firmware dtb0 (T-NKLDEUC 2743.0 dtb.bin, nikel-2G,
sha256 0189cc94):
  mcirb@9c1300: reg=<0x009c1300 0x20>, GIC SPI 110
  mcirs@9c1400: reg=<0x009c1400 0x20>, GIC SPI 111

Both DT nodes are status = "disabled".  Drivers are:
  CONFIG_SDP_MICOM_IRB=m  (samsung,sdp-mc-irb)
  CONFIG_SDP_MICOM_IRS=m  (samsung,sdp-mc-irs)

Built as =m so they never load on the TV.  Full implementation
requires sdp_micom_irb.c (335 lines) and sdp_micom_irs.c (372 lines)
from the GPL source tree (gpl/src/).

Signed-off-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HFSjk2L7MPX5r9CMRGhqwJ
